    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12110" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπῐθέω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πείθω</span>) 
			Ep.
		 form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπειθέω,</span> c. dat.,
		freq. in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> usu. with neg., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀπίθησε
		μύθῳ</span> he <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>disobeyed</i> not the words, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.220
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				6.102
			</span></i>,al.: abs., ib.<i><span class="en">
				16.458
			</span></i>: once c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἀπίθησε θεὰ . . ἀγγελιάων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Cer.</u>
					448
				</span></i>
			: used in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1447
			</span></i> (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>fail to persuade,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἀπίθησέ νιν </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝιν</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Herm.
			</span></i>) <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.36
			</span></i>.</div>
